size_flags_vertical = 3

[node name="IntroContent" type="RichTextLabel" parent="IntroPanel/IntroVBox/IntroScroll"]
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme_override_font_sizes/normal_font_size = 16
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[color=#aabbcc][center][b]🎓 WHAT YOU'LL LEARN[/b][/center]

Encryption is the backbone of cybersecurity. There are two main types:

[color=#00ffff][b]🔑 SYMMETRIC ENCRYPTION[/b][/color]
Uses [color=#ffcc00]ONE shared secret key[/color] for both encryption AND decryption.
• Like a padlock where both people have the same key
• [b]Fast[/b] — great for encrypting large files and data
• [b]Problem:[/b] How do you safely share the key?
• Examples: AES, DES, 3DES, Blowfish, ChaCha20

[color=#ff88ff][b]🔐 ASYMMETRIC ENCRYPTION (Public-Key)[/b][/color]
Uses a [color=#ffcc00]PUBLIC key + PRIVATE key pair[/color] — different keys!
• Public key encrypts → only the private key can decrypt
• [b]Slower[/b] — used for key exchange and signatures
• [b]Solves[/b] the key distribution problem!
• Examples: RSA, ECC, Diffie-Hellman, ElGamal, DSA

[color=#88ff88][center][b]🎮 HOW TO PLAY[/b][/center][/color]

Each wave presents items for you to classify:

[color=#ffcc00]Wave 1:[/color] Sort algorithms → Is it Symmetric or Asymmetric?
[color=#ffcc00]Wave 2:[/color] Match properties → Which type has this trait?
[color=#ffcc00]Wave 3:[/color] Real-world scenarios → Which encryption fits?
[color=#ffcc00]Wave 4:[/color] Challenge questions → Test your knowledge!
[color=#ffcc00]Wave 5:[/color] Final mixed challenge → Everything combined!

[color=#ff8888]❤️ You have 3 hearts. Wrong answers cost a heart!
🔥 Build combos for bonus points!
🏆 Complete all 5 waves to earn maximum XP![/color]

[center][color=#88ff88][b]Read the hints carefully — they teach you the concepts![/b][/color][/center][/color]"
fit_content = true
scroll_active = false

