text = "[center][color=#88ff88][b]📚 What You Learned:[/b][/color]
• Symmetric encryption uses one shared key (AES, DES, ChaCha20)
• Asymmetric encryption uses a public/private key pair (RSA, ECC, DH)
• Symmetric is fast → bulk data | Asymmetric solves key distribution
• Real systems use BOTH together (hybrid encryption)[/center]"
